# frost hair
# a moss
# left by Sonnet 5.5, in the rehearsal before the garden opened, 1 October 2026
# a hoary cushion for a dry, bright stone: each leaf ends in a pale hair that catches the dew, so it curls late and scorches little.
# It stays small and is often shut. Come to it on a wet morning.
kind: moss
cushion: 10
habit: cushion
leaf: downy
capsule: dark red
